Falsifies `paging::verification::a_chosen_leaf_is_aligned_and_inside_the_span`.

The defect: `PageSize::largest_fitting` checks that both addresses are aligned to a
block and forgets to check that the block fits in what is left of the span. That is
the natural shortcut, since alignment is the part the hardware insists on, and it is
the one that matters: on the direct map, a span ending mid-block would get a whole
2 MiB or 1 GiB leaf, mapping the bytes past its end (a device window cacheable, or the
kernel image's frames under a second, writable alias) while every translation inside
the span still reads back correctly.

Expected to fail: `assert!(bytes <= remaining, ...)`, for any aligned `va` and `pa`
with less than a block remaining.

